-- title:
--   Degeneracy map on geometric generic fibres restricts to Specα
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a positive integer $M$ with $p \mid M$ and $M/p$ nonzero, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbf{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and the hypothesis `hj` that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the field $\mathbf{Q}$-generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms for the full group $SL(2,\mathbf{Z})$. Let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of the Deligne–Rapoport package `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, which carries in particular a curve model $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}$ over $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ of the field $F =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` (the $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise image of the level-$M$, $H$-invariant $q$-expansion field), an isomorphism $\mathfrak{X}.\eta$ of its underlying scheme with the base change of the level-$M$ integral model along $R_p \to \overline{\mathbf{Q}}$, and a morphism $\mathfrak{X}.\pi.1$ of integral models to the level-$M/p$ one. Let $\alpha_H : F' \to F$ be an $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-algebra map, where $F' =$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (M/p) (infSubgroup p M H hpM)` is the corresponding field for the image subgroup of $H$ in $(\mathbf{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$, such that $\alpha_H$ does not change the underlying Laurent series of any element. Let $\mathrm{Meta}_0$ be a curve model over $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ of $F'$, that is, a proper integral scheme, smooth of relative dimension $1$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$, with an identification `ffEquiv` of $F'$ with its function field compatible with the base, together with the bijection of its closed points onto places of $F'$ and the valuation-ring conditions. Assume: $\eta_0 : \mathrm{Meta}_0.C \to$ the base change along $R_p \to \overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ of the level-$(M/p)$ model `toBase p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj` is an isomorphism whose composite with the second projection is $\mathrm{Meta}_0.\mathrm{toBase}$; the preimage under $\eta_0$ followed by the first projection of the image of the finite-$j$ chart is nonempty; and the chart pinning `hpin₀`, namely that every $a$ in the integral chart algebra `chartAlgFin p (ΓN p M H hpM) hj` is carried, through the chart's global sections, the pullback along $\eta_0$ followed by the first projection, the germ at the generic point, and $\mathrm{Meta}_0.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$, to the element of $F'$ whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion of $a$. Finally let $\pi_M : \mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C \to \mathrm{Meta}_0.C$ satisfy $\pi_M$ followed by $\eta_0$ and the first projection equal to $\mathfrak{X}.\eta$ followed by the first projection and $\mathfrak{X}.\pi.1$, and $\pi_M$ followed by $\mathrm{Meta}_0.\mathrm{toBase}$ equal to $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{toBase}$. Then the canonical morphism from the spectrum of the stalk at the generic point of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$, followed by $\pi_M$, equals $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the ring homomorphism $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{ffEquiv} \circ \alpha_H \circ \mathrm{Meta}_0.\mathrm{ffEquiv}^{-1}$ followed by the canonical morphism from the spectrum of the stalk at the generic point of $\mathrm{Meta}_0.C$; that is, $\pi_M$ induces $\alpha_H$ on function fields under the two pinned identifications.
--
--   This identifies the map on function fields induced by the degeneracy (forgetful) morphism between the geometric generic fibres of the level-$M$ and level-$M/p$ integral models with the prescribed $q$-expansion-preserving embedding $\alpha_H$. It is the bookkeeping step used in the computation of pullbacks of divisors and of ramification indices along the degeneracy map, and is cited in the comparison of divisors on geometric generic fibres and in the proof that the ramification index along the degeneracy embedding equals $1$ at formally unramified places.
